WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.217 --> 00:00:02.009
STEPHANIE WONG: Hi.

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:02.670
I'm Stephanie.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.530
And today, I'll show
you how Google Cloud's

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.330
visual inspection
products can help

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.850
you improve the efficiency
of the manufacturing

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.580
visual quality
control processes.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.490
In the world of manufacturing,
current market volatility

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.980
leads to huge
operational pressures.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.630
You're first in line
to respond quickly

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.540
to decreased demand,
disruption in the supply chain,

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.670
and interrupted retail channels.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.890
Business continuity
becomes P zero,

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.040
and the weight of reducing
costs falls on your shoulders.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.009
Naturally, leveraging AI
to improve work efficiency

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:33.840
becomes the light at
the end of the tunnel

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.930
as you start to explore more
ways to advance automation,

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.420
control manufacturing
processes remotely,

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.430
and enable a remote workforce.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.250
In the last several years,
visual inspection technologies

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.080
have been helping
manufacturers ease

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.940
these operational pressures.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.520
Image recognition is being
used for electronic part

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.880
classification, retail quality
assurance, and even food

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.410
inspection.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.780
Yet, it can be difficult
and costly to implement

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.190
these technologies.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.110
Traditional inspection
machinery can cost

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.260
millions of dollars per device.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.430
Setting up and deploying
AI for inspection

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.220
not only needs a reliable
IT infrastructure and expert

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.130
resources, but there's usually
a limited amount of sample data

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.510
to start with.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.490
On top of that,
training ML models

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.010
can be extremely
challenging, time consuming,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.620
and can require a specialized
skill set that not

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.330
all companies have access to.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.670
Take these defective
parts, for instance.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.710
Factory workers are
often tasked with finding

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.290
these discrete defects
on the production line.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.540
These small marks can
be extremely subtle,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.270
making it hard for even a
human eye to be able to see.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.100
It's no surprise that
this process can be

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.170
time consuming and inefficient.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.270
This is why Google Cloud
has a rich offering

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.010
for visual inspection
products, which

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.520
reduces the pressure on ground
workers and AI developers

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.470
and increases time to value.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.050
It optimizes for several
steps at the visual inspection

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:53.460
process from data ingestion to
production model optimization.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.950
Google Cloud's visual
inspection products do this

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.750
by enabling customers
to efficiently

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.810
pre-process minimal
images for model training,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:04.080
then it augments the data
and trains automatically,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.120
so you can quickly
deploy the model locally

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.669
and run inferencing at
the production line.

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:11.400
Better yet, you can
continuously improve the model

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.980
by using fresh data collected
from production lines

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.200
to retrain the model
in the cloud giving you

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.230
increased accuracy as you
discover new use cases.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.810
Here's what an end-to-end
architecture would look like.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.090
Once a camera is set up
on the production line,

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.920
users can collect
images and store them

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.600
on the factory floor server.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.250
From here, the
images are uploaded

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.490
to Google Cloud using the visual
inspection AI products to begin

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.170
model training.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.270
Let's say you want to
inspect an assembled product

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.000
to find defective components
like damaged glass on devices.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.270
Labeling thousands of
devices is probably

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.980
the last thing you want to do.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.310
Instead, using Google Cloud's
visual inspection AI products,

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.950
you can upload images for
a new product component,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.390
and the solution
can automatically

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:54.840
extract this component after
you label a few images.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.000
The model will analyze
all loaded images

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.210
to automatically identify the
subset of the data with defects

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.800
or anomalies.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.230
Along the way, you have a
chance to review current model

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.390
performance for
defect detection using

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.420
built-in metrics, like
average precision, precision,

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.980
and recall.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.190
After downloading and
deploying the trained model,

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.180
inferencing can be
efficiently done locally

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.660
on your factory floor for
rapid edge performance.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.640
And when an unlabeled
image comes in,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.970
the deployed model can predict
new defects automatically.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.070
Results can then be viewed
in the central cloud

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.620
dashboard giving prediction
details and a place

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.390
to correct inspections.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.760
Using Google Cloud's
visual inspection products

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.100
you can train
customized ML models

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.280
in the cloud with minimum
amount of label images,

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.110
leverage scalable
cloud infrastructure

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.740
for distributed training
and optimize costs,

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.460
enable production workloads
within weeks versus months,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.080
efficiently deploy
models, and run

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.220
inferencing at production lines
on-premise for low latency.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.800
And it's not just useful
for automating the detection

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.630
of defective devices.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.610
Google Cloud's visual
inspection products

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.280
can support a wide range of
discrete manufacturing use

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.940
cases, such as cosmetic
defect detection and Edge

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.940
detection for electronics,
surface quality

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:12.180
control for automotives,
optical wave for a defect

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.019
detection for semiconductors,
and fabric or packaging quality

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:18.209
control for consumer
packaged goods.

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:20.579
Using Google Cloud's
visual inspection products,

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:23.430
you can increase the throughput
and efficiency of your ML

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.520
models, improve
overall operations,

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.130
and augment your workers
ability to guarantee

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.780
the highest quality
products land

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.910
in the hands of your customer.

